 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573025 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9c394b9f-6048-5783-92f0-54029edfc805" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573038 #edb/ref 1080 "$a=1$, $b=1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573038 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573038 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a8182fdd-de15-5e8d-8c00-cb4f705d6762" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573070 #edb/ref 1080 "-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573070 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573070 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c1265443-5be8-5777-968a-4182b947a1fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573100 #edb/ref 1080 "a=10,\\,b=6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573100 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573100 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dac71056-0aeb-532e-9751-c9f0ed2d8b24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573126 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573126 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573126 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "edcc4ee6-05fd-5ebf-b244-ad7bff1272ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573137 #edb/ref 1080 "a=10,\\,b=3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573137 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573137 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f72d59a7-8c21-5f28-9b5d-e6e72fd46085" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573205 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186572856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573205 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186572919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573205 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573205 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573205 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573205 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573205 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573205 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186572856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573205 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "94c40397-9482-5a52-b940-12d808c2acb6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573225 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186572831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573225 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186572862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573225 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186572988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573225 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573225 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573225 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573225 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573225 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186573038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573225 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cb13aea9-bc77-5453-9aea-bf5b7e71380f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573249 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186572880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573249 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186572931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573249 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573006 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573249 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573249 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186573137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573249 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573249 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573249 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186572931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573249 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ff468151-5610-57e8-a342-0015e9de243b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573251 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573205 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573251 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80840" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573251 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573251 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that a function $f(x,y,z)$ and all of its higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ and that\n\n$$\n{f}_{zx}(x,y,z)=-\\frac{2yz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\\,{f}_{yz}(x,y,z)=\\frac{2xz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate the following expression at the point $(1,2,1):$\n\n$$\n{f}_{zyy}(x,y,z)+{f}_{xxz}(x,y,z)\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573251 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0032ce9b-c24d-5a4a-8814-0479ffd35234" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573251 #edb/ref 1074 "As the higher-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. \n\nHence, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{zyy}(x,y,z) & ={f}_{yzy}(x,y,z) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{yz}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{2xz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4xyz}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn addition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxz}(x,y,z) & ={f}_{zxx}(x,y,z) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{zx}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\frac{2yz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4xyz}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{zyy}(x,y,z)+{f}_{xxz}(x,y,z)=-\\frac{4xyz}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}+\\frac{4xyz}{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{2}}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{f}_{zyy}(1,2,1)+{f}_{xxz}(1,2,1)=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573285 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573225 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573285 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80650" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573285 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573285 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =a{y}^{3}{e}^{x-1}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1}, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & ={x}^{3}{e}^{y-1}+3b{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}, \\\\ {f}_{x}(1,1) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573285 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "71adc372-d2f3-5857-a2ad-a0dc4396f12a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573285 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(a{y}^{3}{e}^{x-1}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1}) \\\\  & =3a{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1} \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{e}^{y-1}+3b{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1}+3b{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1} &=3{x}^{2}{e}^{y-1}+3b{y}^{2}{e}^{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of ${y}^{2}{e}^{x-1},$ respectively, we see that $a=b.$ \n\nSince ${f}_{x}(1,1)=4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,1) & =4 \\\\ a(1)^{3}{e}^{0}+3(1)^{2}{e}^{0} & =4 \\\\ a+3 & =4 \\\\ a & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\nb=a=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573326 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573326 #edb/ref 1069 "q-133220" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573326 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573326 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Find the values of $a$ and $b$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =2ax{y}^{2}-4xy+15x, \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =b{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-4y, \\\\ {f}_{y}(-1,-1) & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573326 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fcbd8ac8-2f1b-5dcb-9ac1-2425c8503e58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573326 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the mixed partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2ax{y}^{2}-4xy+15x) \\\\  & =4axy-4x-0 \\\\  & =4axy-4x \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(b{x}^{2}y-2{x}^{2}-4y) \\\\  & =2bxy-4x-0 \\\\  & =2bxy-4x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal. Hence, we have the identity\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4axy-4x &=2bxy-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $xy$, we see that $a=\\frac{b}{2}.$ \n\nNow, since ${f}_{y}(-1,-1)=-5$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(-1,-1) & =-5 \\\\ b(-1)^{2}(-1)-2(-1)^{2}-4(-1) & =-5 \\\\ -b-2+4 & =-5 \\\\ b & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na=\\frac{b}{2}=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
